<title>Creating a new network</title>
</head>
<body bgcolor="#ffffff">
<h1><img src="../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c2_32.gif" border="0"
	height="32" width="32" hspace="0">&nbsp;Creating a new network</h1>
<hr size="2" align="left" color="blue" width="100%">
<h4>Creating a new network</h4>
<p><strong>Try it now</strong> by following the steps below. After
you have created your new network , you will see its graphical
representation in the network area but now you will only see a blank
window drawing area.</p>
<ol>
	<li>Choose "New Network" from the File Menu or press <img
		vspace="2" src="../../images/carmenIcons/new.gif" border="1"
		height="18" width="17" hspace="2"> "New network" icon on the
	upper side toolbar.</li>
	<li>The "Network Properties" dialog box will appear with the
	"Definition" tab activated.<br>
	<img
		src="../../images/screens/Network Properties Definition Screen.jpg"
		vspace="2" hspace="2"></li>
	<li>Type a name for the new network (this name will be also the
	default name for the network file when saved).</li>
	<li>In this definition panel, you can set values for the Network
	Type and a comment</li>
	<li>You must click on the "Variables" tab.<br>
	<img src="../../images/screens/Network Properties Variables Screen.jpg"
		vspace="2" hspace="2"></li>
	<li>Then you must select the variable type (only Discrete in this
	version, and also Continuous in the next versions) and the Default
	states for the nodes.</li>
	<li>Then, finally, if required, you have the possibility to set up
	other properties in the "Other Properties" tab, with an intuitive set
	of navigation buttons and with a facility to edit directly on the table<br>
	<img
		src="../../images/screens/Network Properties Other Properties Screen.jpg"
		vspace="2" hspace="2"></li>
	<li>Press Ok to create the new node.</li>
</ol>
<p>Each node in the network will have its own properties as it will
show later.&nbsp;</p>
</body>
</html>
